From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:36:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: the player's sound and view camera follow the seat;
 SRNP_TRACE, SRNP_WATCH

The game treats the racers whose index (+0x1029) is below the player
count as "the player"; on a 1P machine that is racer 0 everywhere. The
minimap's index remap (three words of code in low memory: lbz,
addi -seat, blr) becomes a list, now with two paths of the race logic
that only touch presentation:
- 0x80453300 (racer events, 0x8045390C): a sound for the player, and
  the frame of the last such sound (only read by the same "once a
  frame" sound code);
- 0x805735EC (0x80574608): two bytes of the player's view camera.
Left as the game has them until understood: 0x80484A3C (a per-player
task's state) and 0x8054E644 (an effect from the player's camera, then
a per-player table); the paths that create tasks (the heap would differ
from machine to machine) or touch a racer's position are not changed.
Set with the HUD; SRNP_JOUEUR=0 keeps only the minimap's.

Tools: SRNP_TRACE=<addresses> logs which racer takes a path (host
hooks; only seen while the function runs in the interpreter),
SRNP_WATCH=<addresses> logs guest words when they change, read at the
head of the game's frame.

Measured: 8 runners on one PC, each its own seat, a full race: 142
checksums equal, 0 divergences. Neither path happened in the test races,
so their effect is not seen yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
